data-start="0" data-end="141">Here’s a draft catalogue-style entry you could pair with your poem and illustration. It frames the bookshelf as both object and commentary:</p>
<hr data-start="143" data-end="146">
<h2 data-start="148" data-end="216">Catalogue Entry: <em data-start="168" data-end="214">Coran Cubic Orthohedron Rectangular and Neat</em></h2>
<p data-start="218" data-end="480"><strong data-start="218" data-end="229">Object:</strong> Two-sided bookshelf, dimensions 3 × 2 × 19.<br data-start="273" data-end="276">
<strong data-start="276" data-end="291">Provenance:</strong> Conceptual design accompanying the assertion that Job 31:33 is the oldest written verse.<br data-start="380" data-end="383">
<strong data-start="383" data-end="396">Function:</strong> Housing six scrolls (three daily, three evening) to be read over a Metonic cycle.</p>
<h3 data-start="482" data-end="499">Description</h3>
<p data-start="500" data-end="944">This bookshelf is conceived as an <strong data-start="534" data-end="558">orthohedral mnemonic</strong>. Its proportions—three across, two deep, nineteen high—echo ritual cycles of time and text. Three compartments on each face correspond to morning and evening readings; the dual sides reinforce polarity (light/dark, revelation/concealment); the nineteen-unit height recalls the metonic reconciliation of lunar and solar years, as well as the symbolic numerics of scriptural tradition.</p>
<h3 data-start="946" data-end="966">Interpretation</h3>
<p data-start="967" data-end="1282">The object enacts the Job 31:33 injunction to <strong data-start="1013" data-end="1051">conceal, delay, and ration meaning</strong>. Just as the verse commands the covering of “closing arguments,” the bookshelf withholds total access by its very geometry. It is not an archive of abundance, but a rationing device: to pace, defer, and structure interpretation.</p>
<p data-start="1284" data-end="1371">The title <em data-start="1294" data-end="1340">Coran Cubic Orthohedron Rectangular and Neat</em> underscores its dual nature:</p>
<ul data-start="1372" data-end="1550">
<li data-start="1372" data-end="1421">
<p data-start="1374" data-end="1421"><em data-start="1374" data-end="1381">Coran</em> = recitation and collection (<em data-start="1411" data-end="1417">أقرأ</em>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1422" data-end="1472">
<p data-start="1424" data-end="1472"><em data-start="1424" data-end="1443">Cubic Orthohedron</em> = strict, orthogonal form.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1473" data-end="1550">
<p data-start="1475" data-end="1550"><em data-start="1475" data-end="1497">Rectangular and Neat</em> = order imposed upon the mess of drafts and waste.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="1552" data-end="1570">Significance</h3>
<p data-start="1571" data-end="1815">This design fuses <strong data-start="1589" data-end="1644">textual instruction, ritual practice, and carpentry</strong> into a single commentary. The bookshelf is not merely storage but a material metaphor for restraint: a spatialization of the imperative <em data-start="1781" data-end="1813">¡أقرأ! / ¡Hold Back Your Seed!</em></p>
<hr data-start="1817" data-end="1820">
<p data-start="1822" data-end="2024" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to also render this in a <strong data-start="1865" data-end="1895">LaTeX catalogue note style</strong> (like a museum catalogue or scholarly appendix), so you could drop it straight into your monograph alongside the poem and verse?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.07