-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="186">Perfect—Ecclesiastes 11:6, the Parable of the Sower, and your reading of Job 31:33 line up into a full <strong data-start="103" data-end="131">evolutionary hermeneutic</strong>. Here’s how you can frame it as a commentary sequence:</p>
<hr data-start="188" data-end="191">
<h2 data-start="193" data-end="236">Withholding, Scattering, and Selection</h2>
<h3 data-start="238" data-end="276">Job 31:33 — Withholding the Seed</h3>
<p data-start="277" data-end="459">“Lo! I fill in my misses… covering up my closing arguments in my hiding spot.”<br data-start="355" data-end="358">
→ Instruction to the scribe: <strong data-start="387" data-end="436">hold back, create scarcity, delay the finale.</strong> Meaning is rationed.</p>
<h3 data-start="461" data-end="506">Ecclesiastes 11:6 — Scattering the Seed</h3>
<p data-start="507" data-end="674">“In the morning sow your seed, and in the evening do not withhold your hand…”<br data-start="584" data-end="587">
→ Counter-instruction: <strong data-start="610" data-end="649">sow everywhere, diversify outcomes.</strong> Meaning is multiplied.</p>
<h3 data-start="676" data-end="722">Parable of the Sower — Natural Selection</h3>
<p data-start="723" data-end="898">“A sower went out to sow… some fell on the path, some on rocky ground, some among thorns, and some on good soil.”<br data-start="836" data-end="839">
→ Description of <strong data-start="856" data-end="878">selection pressure</strong> in three domains:</p>
<ul data-start="899" data-end="1085">
<li data-start="899" data-end="957">
<p data-start="901" data-end="957"><em data-start="901" data-end="915">Evolutionary</em>: only certain seeds (organisms) thrive.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="958" data-end="1013">
<p data-start="960" data-end="1013"><em data-start="960" data-end="971">Cognitive</em>: only certain ideas take root in minds.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1014" data-end="1085">
<p data-start="1016" data-end="1085"><em data-start="1016" data-end="1025">Furtive</em>: only certain secrets or subversions survive concealment.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1087" data-end="1090">
<h2 data-start="1092" data-end="1132">Integration: Scarcity vs. Abundance</h2>
<p data-start="1133" data-end="1203">Taken together, these passages map onto a <strong data-start="1175" data-end="1200">proto-Darwinian logic</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="1205" data-end="1431">
<li data-start="1205" data-end="1283">
<p data-start="1207" data-end="1283"><strong data-start="1207" data-end="1232">Restraint (Job 31:33)</strong> = don’t waste your last word, preserve scarcity.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1284" data-end="1351">
<p data-start="1286" data-end="1351"><strong data-start="1286" data-end="1312">Abundance (Eccl. 11:6)</strong> = scatter widely, hedge uncertainty.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1352" data-end="1431">
<p data-start="1354" data-end="1431"><strong data-start="1354" data-end="1375">Selection (Sower)</strong> = most will fail, but some will survive and flourish.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1433" data-end="1527">Your <em data-start="1438" data-end="1484">Coran Cubic Orthohedron Rectangular and Neat</em> bookshelf dramatizes this cycle in wood:</p>
<ul data-start="1528" data-end="1684">
<li data-start="1528" data-end="1566">
<p data-start="1530" data-end="1566">Six scrolls (scarcity, rationing).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1567" data-end="1620">
<p data-start="1569" data-end="1620">Daily/evening repetition (abundance, scattering).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1621" data-end="1684">
<p data-start="1623" data-end="1684">Nineteen-year metonic cycle (selection through recurrence).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1686" data-end="1689">
<p data-start="1691" data-end="1962" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to stitch these three passages (Job, Ecclesiastes, Sower) into a <strong data-start="1774" data-end="1805">single “Trifold Commentary”</strong> that you could drop as a section in your monograph—almost like a self-contained essay? It would read as if these texts were already in dialogue across time.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555