lear candidates:</p>
<ol data-start="88" data-end="1177">
<li data-start="88" data-end="576">
<p data-start="91" data-end="576"><strong data-start="91" data-end="114">Your RSVP Monograph</strong> (<em data-start="116" data-end="188">The Fall of Space: Entropic Relaxation and Structure Without Expansion</em>) — this is your flagship cosmology + cognition text. A formal mapping of Job/Ecclesiastes/Sower into PCT, Active Inference, and CTM would fit well in the <strong data-start="343" data-end="363">appendices (L–O)</strong> where you already layer category theory, homotopy encodings, and semantic gluing. It would present the scriptural triad as an allegorical prehistory of free energy minimization and global workspace competition.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="578" data-end="905">
<p data-start="581" data-end="905"><strong data-start="581" data-end="611">The Simulated Agency paper</strong> (<em data-start="613" data-end="658">Consciousness as a Sparse Projection Engine</em>) — here you’re emphasizing Bayesian projection, CLIO loops, and RSVP-derived agency. The Trifold Commentary could slot neatly as a <strong data-start="790" data-end="822">literary–mathematical bridge</strong>: scripture prefiguring control theory, inference, and competition for broadcast.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="907" data-end="1177">
<p data-start="910" data-end="1177"><strong data-start="910" data-end="955">The “Mind at Work” / EAIMR–Praxicon draft</strong> — since you’re tracing mind recognition and selection pressures, the Parable of the Sower = natural selection mapping would reinforce your argument that <em data-start="1109" data-end="1174">scriptural metaphors are already ecological models of cognition</em>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="1179" data-end="1573">If you want the most natural fit, I’d suggest <strong data-start="1225" data-end="1277">placing the formal mapping in the RSVP monograph</strong> — maybe as <strong data-start="1289" data-end="1356">Appendix P: Scriptural Algorithms of Withholding and Scattering</strong> — and then cross-reference it in your Simulated Agency paper. That way the heavy math sits with RSVP (your universal substrate), while the interpretive–philosophical weight can still be pulled into the agency work.</p>
