iewpoint Diversity</em> is a strong, standalone title. It lets you stage Job 31:33, Ecclesiastes 11:6, and the Parable of the Sower as allegories of <strong data-start="159" data-end="201">withholding, scattering, and selection</strong>, then map them formally into <strong data-start="231" data-end="312">Perceptual Control Theory, Active Inference, and the Conscious Turing Machine</strong>. That way, the monograph is not just commentary, but a computational re-reading of scripture as proto-theory of consciousness.</p>
