</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\geometry</span></span><span>{margin=1in}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\title</span></span><span>{Viewpoint Diversity: Scriptural Algorithms of Withholding, Scattering, and Selection}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\author</span></span><span>{Flyxion}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\date</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\today</span></span><span>}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{document}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\maketitle</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{abstract}
This monograph interprets three scriptural passages---Job 31:33, Ecclesiastes 11:6, and the Parable of the Sower---as proto-computational models of consciousness. Job instructs withholding, Ecclesiastes scattering, and the Sower selection. These imperatives map naturally to control theory, active inference, and the Conscious Turing Machine (CTM). The result is a unified hermeneutic: viewpoint diversity as a balance between scarcity, abundance, and selective revelation.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{abstract}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Introduction}
We propose that the oldest written verse, Job 31:33, is not primarily moral but editorial: an instruction to withhold the denouement, to ration interpretation. Read alongside Ecclesiastes 11:6 and the Parable of the Sower, these texts encode a cycle of withholding, scattering, and selection. This cycle anticipates modern computational theories of perception and consciousness.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{The Scriptural Triad}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Job 31:33 --- Withholding}
Text and translation. Interpretation as scarcity principle.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Ecclesiastes 11:6 --- Scattering}
Text and translation. Interpretation as abundance principle.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Parable of the Sower --- Selection}
Text and parable. Interpretation as selection principle.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Formal Mapping}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Perceptual Control Theory (PCT)}
Equations for control error and withholding gate.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Active Inference}
Free energy, expected free energy, entropy-augmented policy selection.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Parable of the Sower as Bayesian Selection}
Seeds as hypotheses, soil as likelihood, posterior fitness.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Conscious Turing Machine (CTM)}
Competition, broadcast, Brainish codebook.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Integration}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Withhold </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> control loops suppress premature disclosure.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Scatter </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> maintain high entropy priors under uncertainty.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Select </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> Bayesian updating under environmental constraints.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}
We define viewpoint diversity as the dynamic equilibrium of these three imperatives.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Implications}
Links to contemporary models:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Active inference and predictive processing.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Perceptual control theory and recursive agency.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Conscious Turing Machine and broadcast competition.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}
Scripture anticipates these principles as editorial law: interpretive scarcity, exploratory abundance, and selective survival.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Conclusion}
Viewpoint diversity arises when interpretation is withheld, scattered, and selected in balanced proportion. This cycle unites ancient textual instructions with modern theories of cognition, grounding consciousness in the economy of meaning itself.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{document}
