t — here’s the extended <strong data-start="32" data-end="47">Chapter X+2</strong>, now with explicit <strong data-start="67" data-end="117">mathematical and computational correspondences</strong> woven into Joseph’s silos and the snake’s shedding. This way the chapter stays essayistic but deepens into the same formal register as Chapter X+1.</p>
<hr data-start="269" data-end="272">
<h1 data-start="274" data-end="332"><strong data-start="276" data-end="330">Chapter X+2 — Silos and Skins: Survival as Reading</strong></h1>
<p data-start="334" data-end="796">The cycle of <em data-start="347" data-end="354">iqraʾ</em>—to gather, to pattern, to return, to withhold, to incubate, to renew, to endure—does not remain in the abstract. It takes flesh in the survival strategies of both humans and animals. Language encodes cognition, but cognition itself is nothing other than the management of scarcity and abundance. Thus the philological meanings of reading can be interpreted equally as injunctions to store grain, to shed skins, to hold back and to release.</p>
<hr data-start="798" data-end="801">
<h3 data-start="803" data-end="853"><strong data-start="807" data-end="851">Joseph’s Silos: Withholding as Foresight</strong></h3>
<p data-start="854" data-end="1197">When Joseph interprets Pharaoh’s dream of fat and lean cows, he prescribes a policy: store grain in silos during years of plenty, so that famine years may be endured. Here the fifth meaning of <em data-start="1047" data-end="1054">iqraʾ</em>—to become pregnant, to retain—translates into agricultural infrastructure. Reading is storing. To withhold is not miserliness but foresight.</p>
<p data-start="1199" data-end="1242">In <strong data-start="1202" data-end="1220">control theory</strong>, this is buffering:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{t+1} = B_t + y_t - c_t,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8917em; vertical-align: -0.2083em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0502em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0502em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">y</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1280" data-end="1439">where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0502em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is the buffer (silo contents), <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">y</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is yield (harvest), and <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5806em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is consumption. Stability requires <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{t+1} \geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8917em; vertical-align: -0.2083em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0502em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span> even under famine.</p>
<p data-start="1441" data-end="1534">In <strong data-start="1444" data-end="1464">active inference</strong>, Joseph’s silos exemplify the minimization of expected free energy:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="double-struck">E</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mtext>risk</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\pi) = \mathbb{E}_{q(o,s \mid \pi)}[-\ln p(o \mid s)] + \text{risk}(\pi),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1052em; vertical-align: -0.3552em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3448em;"><span style="top: -2.5198em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span><span class="mopen mtight">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">o</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">s</span><span class="mrel mtight">∣</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="mclose mtight">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3552em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop">ln</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">o</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">s</span><span class="mclose">)]</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">risk</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1621" data-end="1690">where policies <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span></span></span></span> that stockpile resources reduce future risk.</p>
<p data-start="1692" data-end="1770">In the <strong data-start="1699" data-end="1727">Conscious Turing Machine</strong>, silos are parallel to chunk incubation:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⋅</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i,t+1} = w_{i,t} \cdot \alpha + \delta_{i,t},</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7167em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02691em;">w</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0269em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7306em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02691em;">w</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0269em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9805em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">δ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0379em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1830" data-end="1954">where chunk weights <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5806em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02691em;">w</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0269em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> are retained across cycles, increasing their chance of future broadcast when conditions shift.</p>
<p data-start="1956" data-end="2087">Joseph’s silos, then, are not only barns of wheat but archives of meaning: withheld drafts preserved against interpretive famine.</p>
<hr data-start="2089" data-end="2092">
<h3 data-start="2094" data-end="2143"><strong data-start="2098" data-end="2141">The Snake’s Shedding: Renewal as Escape</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2144" data-end="2442">Where Joseph accumulates, the serpent discards. A snake shedding its skin dramatizes the sixth meaning of <em data-start="2250" data-end="2257">iqraʾ</em>: to menstruate, to shed blood, to renew. Shedding here is not only release but transformation: the animal leaves behind a husk, an old identity, in order to continue life unburdened.</p>
<p data-start="2444" data-end="2525">In <strong data-start="2447" data-end="2476">Perceptual Control Theory</strong>, this corresponds to <strong data-start="2498" data-end="2522">resetting references</strong>:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>r</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>with&nbsp;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>r</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>chosen&nbsp;to&nbsp;minimize&nbsp;persistent&nbsp;error</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t+1} = r_t + \Delta r, \quad \text{with } \Delta r \;\;\text{chosen to minimize persistent error}.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6389em; vertical-align: -0.2083em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">with&nbsp;</span></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">chosen&nbsp;to&nbsp;minimize&nbsp;persistent&nbsp;error</span></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2638" data-end="2690">If a reference cannot be matched, it is abandoned.</p>
<p data-start="2692" data-end="2754">In <strong data-start="2695" data-end="2715">active inference</strong>, shedding is Bayesian model pruning:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>for&nbsp;unfit&nbsp;models&nbsp;</mtext><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(m_k \mid o_{1:T}) \to 0 \quad \text{for unfit models } m_k,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">o</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span><span class="mrel mtight">:</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">for&nbsp;unfit&nbsp;models&nbsp;</span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2827" data-end="2897">so that cognitive resources are not trapped in maladaptive policies.</p>
<p data-start="2899" data-end="3020">In the <strong data-start="2906" data-end="2913">CTM</strong>, shedding is the downtree collapse: chunks that fail to win broadcast are eliminated, freeing the stage:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>lim</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>broadcast</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>if&nbsp;</mtext><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t \to \infty} \Pr(\text{broadcast}(c_j)) = 0 \quad \text{if } w_j \ll \sum_i w_i.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.45em; vertical-align: -0.7em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6944em;"><span style="top: -2.4em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mrel mtight">→</span><span class="mord mtight">∞</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span><span class="mop">lim</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop">Pr</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">broadcast</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">))</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9805em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">if&nbsp;</span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02691em;">w</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0269em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≪</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.3277em; vertical-align: -1.2777em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.05em;"><span style="top: -1.8723em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op">∑</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.2777em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02691em;">w</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0269em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3119" data-end="3397">The snake also adds a survival nuance: shedding as <strong data-start="3170" data-end="3180">escape</strong>. To slough off a mantle is to evade capture, leaving behind what is graspable so that the living system continues. Consciousness itself may do this—abandoning identities, drafts, or mantles that constrain survival.</p>
<hr data-start="3399" data-end="3402">
<h3 data-start="3404" data-end="3471"><strong data-start="3408" data-end="3469">Integration: Scarcity and Renewal in the Cycle of Reading</strong></h3>
<p data-start="3472" data-end="3680">Together, Joseph’s silos and the snake’s skin recast the cycle of <em data-start="3538" data-end="3545">iqraʾ</em> in ecological time. To <strong data-start="3569" data-end="3578">store</strong> is to guard against scarcity. To <strong data-start="3612" data-end="3620">shed</strong> is to survive through renewal. Both are modes of reading.</p>
<ul data-start="3682" data-end="3842">
<li data-start="3682" data-end="3759">
<p data-start="3684" data-end="3759"><strong data-start="3684" data-end="3706">Silos = incubation</strong>: buffering resources or meanings until their time.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3760" data-end="3842">
<p data-start="3762" data-end="3842"><strong data-start="3762" data-end="3784">Shedding = renewal</strong>: discarding obsolete structures to enable continuation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3844" data-end="3903">The combined law can be expressed as a dual optimization:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mi>π</mi></munder><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(foresight)</mtext><mspace width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width="2em"></mspace><munder><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mi>π</mi></munder><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(renewal)</mtext><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\pi} G(\pi) \quad \text{(foresight)} \qquad \text{and} \qquad \max_{\pi} H(\pi \mid o) \quad \text{(renewal)},</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.45em; vertical-align: -0.7em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6679em;"><span style="top: -2.4em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span><span class="mop">min</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">(foresight)</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 2em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">and</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 2em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.4306em;"><span style="top: -2.4em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span><span class="mop">max</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">o</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">(renewal)</span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4031" data-end="4204">where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> is expected free energy (storage against uncertainty) and <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\pi \mid o)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">o</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> is entropy conditioned on observation (diversity maintained through shedding).</p>
<p data-start="4206" data-end="4312">Scripture thus encodes the double injunction: preserve against famine, and discard to escape constraint.</p>
<hr data-start="4314" data-end="4317">
<h3 data-start="4319" data-end="4355"><strong data-start="4323" data-end="4353">Toward Viewpoint Diversity</strong></h3>
<p data-start="4356" data-end="4614">By extending <em data-start="4369" data-end="4376">iqraʾ</em> into silos and skins, the thesis grounds its philological algorithm in embodied survival. Reading is not merely intellectual but agricultural, animal, ecological. To read is to live through cycles of excess and want, danger and escape.</p>
<p data-start="4616" data-end="4654">The imperative is therefore doubled:</p>
<ul data-start="4655" data-end="4750">
<li data-start="4655" data-end="4702">
<p data-start="4657" data-end="4702"><strong data-start="4657" data-end="4669">Preserve</strong> against the famine of meaning.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4703" data-end="4750">
<p data-start="4705" data-end="4750"><strong data-start="4705" data-end="4713">Shed</strong> against the predation of rigidity.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4752" data-end="5006">Between Joseph and the serpent, between silos and skins, we glimpse what <em data-start="4825" data-end="4846">Viewpoint Diversity</em> means at its deepest: consciousness as the art of survival through withholding and renewal, an economy where nothing is ever final, yet nothing is ever lost.</p>
<hr data-start="5008" data-end="5011">
