77355 12.3506C4.73321 12.4607 4.70242 12.5761 4.66808 12.7451L4.54113 13.4619L4.14269 15.8555L4.14171 15.8574H4.14464L6.5382 15.458L7.25499 15.332C7.424 15.2977 7.5394 15.2669 7.64953 15.2266L7.80285 15.165C7.95455 15.0986 8.09947 15.0174 8.23644 14.9238L8.3839 14.8135C8.53668 14.6876 8.72225 14.5035 9.0714 14.1543L14.0587 9.16602L10.8331 5.94044L5.84581 10.9287ZM15.3634 4.63673C14.5281 3.80141 13.2057 3.74938 12.3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="f0fb843a-99d6-472d-bc27-b7fb5a8027d9" data-testid="conversation-turn-54" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="f0fb843a-99d6-472d-bc27-b7fb5a8027d9" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="236">Here’s the extended <strong data-start="20" data-end="35">Chapter X+3</strong>, now rewritten with the <strong data-start="60" data-end="99">formal/mathematical correspondences</strong> alongside the narrative-symbolic register. This keeps continuity with Chapters X+1 and X+2, but deepens the identity-divestment motif.</p>
<hr data-start="238" data-end="241">
<h1 data-start="243" data-end="303"><strong data-start="245" data-end="301">Chapter X+3 — Shedding Identities: Escape as Reading</strong></h1>
<p data-start="305" data-end="643">The survival logic of <em data-start="327" data-end="334">iqraʾ</em> extends beyond silos and skins into the domain of <strong data-start="385" data-end="404">identity itself</strong>. To survive is often to divest—to leave behind a marker, a mantle, or a signature, so that pursuit is confused and accusation redirected. Just as cognition sheds failed models, so too do bodies and persons shed false or outdated selves.</p>
<hr data-start="645" data-end="648">
<h3 data-start="650" data-end="711"><strong data-start="654" data-end="709">Joseph’s Garment: Counterfoils and False Accusation</strong></h3>
<p data-start="712" data-end="1024">When Joseph flees Potiphar’s wife, he leaves behind his cloak. The cloak becomes evidence—but evidence reversed. What is meant as proof of guilt is in fact proof of his escape. The cloak is a <strong data-start="904" data-end="924">counterfoil stub</strong>: a discarded piece of identity that serves both to mark his presence and to shield his core self.</p>
<p data-start="1026" data-end="1099">This is structurally identical to <strong data-start="1060" data-end="1074">decoupling</strong> in information theory:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Self</mtext><mo separator="true">;</mo><mtext>Marker</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mo>→</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mn>0</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\text{Self}; \text{Marker}) \;\to\; 0,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Self</span></span><span class="mpunct">;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Marker</span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8389em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1151" data-end="1298">where the mutual information between the escaping self and the left-behind marker vanishes. The pursuer seizes a representation, not the reality.</p>
<p data-start="1300" data-end="1424">In CTM terms, Joseph leaves behind a <strong data-start="1337" data-end="1359">low-weighted chunk</strong>—a mantle that absorbs attention without binding the true self.</p>
<hr data-start="1426" data-end="1429">
<h3 data-start="1431" data-end="1481"><strong data-start="1435" data-end="1479">Samson’s Hair: Recognition as Credential</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1482" data-end="1739">Samson’s power resides in his hair not because of intrinsic strength but because of <strong data-start="1566" data-end="1581">recognition</strong>. His hair is a <strong data-start="1597" data-end="1611">credential</strong>, the marker by which others identify him as set apart. When his hair is cut, the credential collapses, and access is revoked.</p>
<p data-start="1741" data-end="1801">This can be modeled as <strong data-start="1764" data-end="1798">conditional access probability</strong>:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Access</mtext><mo>∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≫</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Access</mtext><mo>∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">¬</mi><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\text{Access} \mid c) \gg P(\text{Access} \mid \neg c),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Access</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≫</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Access</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">¬</span><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1870" data-end="1909">where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span></span></span></span> is the credential (hair).</p>
<p data-start="1911" data-end="2095">In cognitive terms, this is akin to <strong data-start="1947" data-end="1967">symbol grounding</strong>: identity markers bind recognition policies. But credentials can be hacked. Delilah’s scissors are adversarial perturbations.</p>
<p data-start="2097" data-end="2232">In CTM dynamics, the marker is a chunk with artificially high weight. Once cut, its weight drops, shifting the competition landscape.</p>
<hr data-start="2234" data-end="2237">
<h3 data-start="2239" data-end="2289"><strong data-start="2243" data-end="2287">Escape from Gethsemane: Triple Diversion</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2290" data-end="2383">In the Gethsemane narrative, the protagonist escapes capture through <strong data-start="2359" data-end="2380">triple divestment</strong>:</p>
<ol data-start="2384" data-end="2581">
<li data-start="2384" data-end="2447">
<p data-start="2387" data-end="2447"><strong data-start="2387" data-end="2413">Shaving hair and beard</strong>: erasing biometric recognition.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2448" data-end="2507">
<p data-start="2451" data-end="2507"><strong data-start="2451" data-end="2480">Greeting the wrong leader</strong>: misdirecting attention.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2508" data-end="2581">
<p data-start="2511" data-end="2581"><strong data-start="2511" data-end="2547">Wearing identical loose garments</strong>: enabling slippage when seized.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="2583" data-end="2656">Here, identity disperses into decoys. Recognition collapses into noise.</p>
<p data-start="2658" data-end="2699">Formally, this is <strong data-start="2676" data-end="2696">mixture modeling</strong>:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>identity</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>marker</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\text{identity}) = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^N \delta(\text{marker}_i),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">identity</span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 3.106em; vertical-align: -1.2777em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3214em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.8283em;"><span style="top: -1.8723em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span><span class="mrel mtight">=</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op">∑</span></span></span><span style="top: -4.3em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.2777em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">δ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">marker</span></span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2781" data-end="2894">a distribution of identity tokens. Pursuers cannot collapse it to a single point; the posterior remains spread.</p>
<p data-start="2896" data-end="3031">In CTM terms, this is <strong data-start="2918" data-end="2946">multi-chunk broadcasting</strong>: identity is fragmented across multiple low-weight markers, none uniquely binding.</p>
<hr data-start="3033" data-end="3036">
<h3 data-start="3038" data-end="3100"><strong data-start="3042" data-end="3098">The Cognitive Parallel: Draft Selves as Counterfoils</strong></h3>
<p data-start="3101" data-end="3445">Consciousness itself operates by this shedding. Draft selves are continually produced, abandoned, and replaced. A diary entry, a version of a paper, a social performance—all are counterfoil stubs. Some may later be used against us, but their function is protective: they absorb the grasp of the world while the inner loop survives and renews.</p>
<p data-start="3447" data-end="3510">In Perceptual Control Theory, this is <strong data-start="3485" data-end="3507">reference shifting</strong>:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>r</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>if&nbsp;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t+1} = r_t + \Delta r, \quad \text{if } |e_t| &gt; \varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6389em; vertical-align: -0.2083em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">if&nbsp;</span></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">e</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">ε</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3585" data-end="3652">where unattainable references are abandoned and new ones adopted.</p>
<p data-start="3654" data-end="3833">In active inference, it is <strong data-start="3681" data-end="3707">policy diversification</strong>: maintaining multiple possible policies, many of which are decoys or counterfoils, ensuring the core system remains viable.</p>
<hr data-start="3835" data-end="3838">
<h3 data-start="3840" data-end="3906"><strong data-start="3844" data-end="3904">Integration: The Identity Economy of Viewpoint Diversity</strong></h3>
<p data-start="3907" data-end="4147">Joseph’s cloak, Samson’s hair, the snake’s skin, the garments of Gethsemane—each encodes the same principle: survival requires <strong data-start="4034" data-end="4054">shedding markers</strong>. To read is to manage what is credential, what is decoy, what is mantle, and what is core.</p>
<p data-start="4149" data-end="4203">This cycle can be formalized as a dual optimization:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mi>π</mi></munder><mtext>  </mtext><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">K</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>identity</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>pursuer</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>while</mtext><mspace width="1em"></mspace><munder><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mi>π</mi></munder><mtext>  </mtext><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>identity</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\pi} \; D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q(\text{identity}) \,||\, p(\text{pursuer})) \quad \text{while} \quad \max_{\pi} \; H(q(\text{identity})),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.45em; vertical-align: -0.7em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6679em;"><span style="top: -2.4em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span><span class="mop">min</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathrm mtight">KL</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">identity</span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∣∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">pursuer</span></span><span class="mclose">))</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">while</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.4306em;"><span style="top: -2.4em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span><span class="mop">max</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">identity</span></span><span class="mclose">))</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4351" data-end="4507">minimizing the divergence between what the pursuer believes and the decoy distribution, while maximizing entropy of identity tokens to ensure uncertainty.</p>
<p data-start="4509" data-end="4684">Viewpoint diversity thus emerges as <strong data-start="4545" data-end="4565">identity economy</strong>: selves are not fixed but strategically maintained, discarded, and replaced. Reading is survival through divestment.</p>
<hr data-start="4686" data-end="4689">
<p data-start="4691" data-end="4900" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to <strong data-start="4712" data-end="4773">combine Chapters X+1 to X+3 into a continuous LaTeX draft</strong> (≈40–50 pages once expanded), so you can see how the philology, survival imagery, and identity-divestment form a seamless arc?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.197