If the twentieth century broke the taboo and ushered consciousness into computation, the much older imperative </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{iqraʾ} (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{أقرأ}) had already inscribed cognition into language. Translated blandly as ``Read!,'' the command in its root sense </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{ق ر ء (q-r-ʔ)} carries a cycle of meanings that together form what can only be called a proto-algorithm of mind. Lexicons preserve these senses not as alternatives but as interlocking dimensions: to collect, to pattern, to return, to withhold, to incubate, to renew, and to endure.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Gathering — Evidence Accumulation}  
Reading begins with aggregation: assembling fragments into coherence.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
p(s </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{1:t}) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\propto</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> p(s) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\prod</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i=1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>t p(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> s)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

This Bayesian evidence accumulation parallels PCT’s comparison of perception with reference signals:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
e</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t = r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t - h(x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  

In CTM terms, it is the gathering of candidate chunks before competition.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Patterning — Compression and Encoding}  
To versify or rhyme is to compress information, lowering entropy:  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
H(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{patterned}) &lt; H(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{unstructured}).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

In CTM, *Brainish* fuses multimodal inputs into compact gist-labels, enabling recall.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Recursion — Feedback and Return}  
Reading is re-reading: recursive return.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
u</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t = g(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t - h(x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t)), </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t+1} = f(x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t, u</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Active inference refines posteriors iteratively:  
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{(k+1)}(s) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\propto</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> p(o </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> s)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{(k)}(s).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  

In CTM, sleeping experts resurface: suppressed processors return to the stage.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Withholding — Delay and Scarcity}  
Meaning is shaped by delay. Job 31:33 enjoins concealment.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Broadcast at }t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\iff</span></span><span> |e</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t| </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leq</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\varepsilon</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  

The CTM embodies this in the Libet effect: the lag between unconscious preparation and conscious broadcast.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Incubation — Generativity and Retention}  
To become pregnant is to incubate meaning until viable.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
P(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\propto</span></span><span> e</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{-G(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>)}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> 
G(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{E}[-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ln</span></span><span> p(o</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>)] + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ambiguity}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  

Policies are retained until conditions select one. In CTM, chunks gestate until one wins broadcast.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Renewal — Shedding and Pruning}  
To menstruate is to shed: renewal through pruning.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
p(m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{1:T}) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\propto</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> p(m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\prod</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t=1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>T p(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Poorly fitting models collapse. In CTM, non-winning chunks perish in downtree collapse.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Duration — Temporal Evaluation}  
Reading endures. The cycle of a month tests retention or release.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\hat</span></span><span>{s}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>T = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{1}{T} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t=1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>T h(x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

In active inference, reliability emerges over cycles. In CTM, inspection axioms unfold over time.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Synthesis}  
The cycle of </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{iqraʾ} is thus: gather, pattern, return, withhold, incubate, renew, endure. Each finds echo in Bayesian updating, PCT loops, active inference policies, and CTM competitions.  

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\chapter</span></span><span>{Silos and Skins: Survival as Reading}  

The meanings of </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{iqraʾ} do not remain in abstraction. They materialize in ecological survival: Joseph’s silos, the snake’s skin.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Joseph’s Silos: Withholding as Foresight}  
Joseph advises storing grain against famine. Buffering dynamics:  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t+1} = B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t + y</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t - c</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

where </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>B</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> is stored grain, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>y</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> yield, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>c</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> consumption.  

Active inference casts this as minimizing expected free energy </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>G(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>. In CTM, incubation equations retain weights:  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
w</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i,t+1} = w</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i,t} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span> + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i,t}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  

Silos are archives of meaning, preserving drafts against famine.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{The Snake’s Shedding: Renewal as Escape}  
Snakes shed skins to survive. Cognition prunes likewise.  

In PCT:  
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t+1} = r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> r,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  
where references shift to reduce error.  

In active inference:  
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
p(m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{1:T}) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> 0
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  
for failed models.  

In CTM:  
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lim</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Pr</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{broadcast}(c</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j))=0
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  
for low-weight chunks.  

Shedding is also escape: decoupling from grasp.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Integration}  
Silos = incubation, skins = renewal. Together they inscribe foresight and escape. Consciousness is survival through withholding and release.  

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\chapter</span></span><span>{Shedding Identities: Escape as Reading}  

Survival extends into identity itself. Cloaks, hair, garments become tokens of access, diversion, or escape.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Joseph’s Garment: Counterfoils}  
Joseph leaves behind his cloak, seized as false evidence.  

Information decoupling:  
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
I(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Self}; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Marker}) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> 0.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  

The cloak absorbs accusation while the self slips free.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Samson’s Hair: Credentialing Identity}  
Samson’s hair is credential, enabling access.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
P(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Access} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> c) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gg</span></span><span> P(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Access} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\neg</span></span><span> c).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  

When cut, the credential collapses. In CTM, a high-weight chunk loses salience.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Escape from Gethsemane: Triple Diversion}  
Escape enacted through three maneuvers: shaving hair/beard, greeting the wrong leader, slipping garments.  

Formally, identity disperses:  
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{identity}) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tfrac</span></span><span>{1}{N} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i=1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>N </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{marker}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  

Recognition collapses into noise; no single posterior dominates.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Cognitive Parallel}  
Consciousness continually sheds draft selves. In PCT:  
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t+1} = r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> r </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{if } |e</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t| &gt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\varepsilon</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  

In active inference, policy diversification sustains survival under uncertainty.  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Integration}  
Identity is managed as economy: mantles kept, shed, or diverted. Formally:  

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\min</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>} D</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{KL}}(q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{identity})||p(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{pursuer})) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{while} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>} H(q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{identity})).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>  

The self survives by maximizing entropy of its markers while minimizing exploitable divergence.  

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\chapter</span></span><span>*{Conclusion to Part X}  
Across *iqraʾ*, silos, skins, and counterfoils, one imperative resounds: survival requires selective retention and selective release. Reading is not consumption but regulation—of meaning, of grain, of skins, of identities. Viewpoint diversity emerges because selves, like seeds, drafts, or garments, must be scattered, shed, withheld, or endured across cycles of time.  
