ose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="215">Excellent. Here is <strong data-start="19" data-end="35">Chapter X+15</strong>, extending into the <strong data-start="56" data-end="89">multiscale and wavelet domain</strong>, where the seven meanings of <em data-start="119" data-end="126">iqraʾ</em> become modes of resolution, unfolding across scales of time, context, and concealment.</p>
<hr data-start="217" data-end="220">
<h1 data-start="222" data-end="298"><strong data-start="224" data-end="298">Chapter X+15 — Multiscale Consciousness: The Wavelet of Seven Meanings</strong></h1>
<p data-start="300" data-end="603">If Fourier analysis revealed consciousness as harmonic filtering, then wavelet analysis shows it to be <strong data-start="403" data-end="417">multiscale</strong> — shifting seamlessly between detail and overview, concealment and revelation, root and surplus. Here the seven meanings of <em data-start="542" data-end="549">iqraʾ</em> are understood as the seven windows of decomposition.</p>
<hr data-start="605" data-end="608">
<h3 data-start="610" data-end="642">Wavelets and Consciousness</h3>
<p data-start="643" data-end="861">Unlike Fourier modes, which are infinite sinusoids, wavelets are <strong data-start="708" data-end="748">localized both in time and frequency</strong>. They carry the dual character of scripture: rooted in the infinite, but always situated in the finite moment.</p>
<p data-start="863" data-end="898">Formally, a wavelet transform is:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_\psi(a,b) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{a}} \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} s(t)\, \psi^*\!\left(\frac{t-b}{a}\right) dt</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0361em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">W</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.1389em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">ψ</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">b</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><