mal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">ψ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7387em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mbin mtight">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner"><span class="mopen delimcenter" style="top: 0em;"><span class="delimsizing size3">(</span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3714em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">b</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mclose delimcenter" style="top: 0em;"><span class="delimsizing size3">)</span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1009" data-end="1058">where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span></span></span></span> sets the scale, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">b</span></span></span></span> the position.</p>
<ul data-start="1060" data-end="1213">
<li data-start="1060" data-end="1146">
<p data-start="1062" data-end="1146"><strong data-start="1062" data-end="1078">Scale <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span></span></span></span>:</strong> how much we zoom in or out (daily vs. metonic, seed vs. harvest).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1147" data-end="1213">
<p data-start="1149" data-end="1213"><strong data-start="1149" data-end="1168">Position <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">b</span></span></span></span>:</strong> where in time we read, recite, or conceal.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1215" data-end="1218">
<h3 data-start="1220" data-end="1264">The Seven Meanings as Multiscale Modes</h3>
<p data-start="1265" data-end="1384">The verb <em data-start="1274" data-end="1281">iqraʾ</em> carries seven dimensions of meaning. In wavelet terms, these are seven <strong data-start="1353" data-end="1381">resolutions of attention</strong>:</p>
<ol data-start="1386" data-end="2006">
<li data-start="1386" data-end="1471">
<p data-start="1389" data-end="1471"><strong data-start="1389" data-end="1405">Read / Study</strong> — fine detail, small scale <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span></span></span></span>. Close inspection of patterns.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1472" data-end="1564">
<p data-start="1475" data-end="1564"><strong data-start="1475" data-end="1503">Collect / Piece Together</strong> — medium scale, assembling patches into a coherent signal.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1565" data-end="1646">
<p data-start="1568" data-end="1646"><strong data-start="1568" data-end="1590">Draw Near / Return</strong> — translation across scales, coming back to overview.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1647" data-end="1739">
<p data-start="1650" data-end="1739"><strong data-start="1650" data-end="1671">Delay / Hold Back</strong> — suppressing coefficients, concealing details at certain scales.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1740" data-end="1826">
<p data-start="1743" data-end="1826"><strong data-start="1743" data-end="1765">Retain (Pregnancy)</strong> — storage at intermediate scales, preserving latent modes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1827" data-end="1922">
<p data-start="1830" data-end="1922"><strong data-start="1830" data-end="1846">Wait a Month</strong> — cyclic scale (metonic), aligning decomposition with calendrical rhythm.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1923" data-end="2006">
<p data-start="1926" data-end="2006"><strong data-start="1926" data-end="1943">Recite / Warn</strong> — broadcast across scales, reconstruction from coefficients.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="2008" data-end="2134">Thus <em data-start="2013" data-end="2020">iqraʾ</em> is a wavelet operator: a command to read reality at multiple resolutions, to compress and expand consciousness.</p>
<hr data-start="2136" data-end="2139">
<h3 data-start="2141" data-end="2179">Concealment as Scale Suppression</h3>
<p data-start="2180" data-end="2252">In wavelet space, concealment is simply <strong data-start="2220" data-end="2249">thresholding coefficients</strong>:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>if&nbsp;below&nbsp;threshold</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_\psi(a,b) \to 0 \quad \text{if below threshold}.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0361em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">W</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.1389em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">ψ</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">b</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">if&nbsp;below&nbsp;threshold</span></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2312" data-end="2455">This is Job’s concealment, Joseph’s storage, the scribe’s withholding: surplus is hidden in higher scales, awaiting the moment of revelation.</p>
<hr data-start="2457" data-end="2460">
<h3 data-start="2462" data-end="2497">Surplus as Multiscale Storage</h3>
<p data-start="2498" data-end="2730">Surplus is not infinite abundance at one scale, but <strong data-start="2550" data-end="2591">distributed energy across many scales</strong>. The grain in silos, the hundredfold harvest, the resonance of song — all are stored coefficients, ready for reconstruction when needed.</p>
<p data-start="2732" data-end="2747">In CTM terms:</p>
<ul data-start="2748" data-end="2850">
<li data-start="2748" data-end="2778">
<p data-start="2750" data-end="2778">STM = fine scale (detail).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2779" data-end="2812">
<p data-start="2781" data-end="2812">LTM = coarse scale (context).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2813" data-end="2850">
<p data-start="2815" data-end="2850">Broadcast = multiscale synthesis.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2852" data-end="2855">
<h3 data-start="2857" data-end="2895">CTM and Multiscale Decomposition</h3>
<p data-start="2896" data-end="2980">The Conscious Turing Machine (CTM) can be seen as a <strong data-start="2948" data-end="2977">wavelet transform machine</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="2981" data-end="3190">
<li data-start="2981" data-end="3053">
<p data-start="2983" data-end="3053">Uptree competition = sparse thresholding of fine-scale coefficients.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3054" data-end="3116">
<p data-start="3056" data-end="3116">Downtree broadcast = reconstruction into global awareness.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3117" data-end="3190">
<p data-start="3119" data-end="3190">Brainish = dictionary of multiscale atoms, fusing detail and context.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3192" data-end="3320">Thus consciousness oscillates: sometimes inspecting detail, sometimes zooming out, always weaving scales into a unitary field.</p>
<hr data-start="3322" data-end="3325">
<h3 data-start="3327" data-end="3363">Scriptural Multiscale Parables</h3>
<ul data-start="3364" data-end="3823">
<li data-start="3364" data-end="3446">
<p data-start="3366" data-end="3446"><strong data-start="3366" data-end="3385">Joseph’s Silos:</strong> storage at coarse scale, later released as reconstruction.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3447" data-end="3550">
<p data-start="3449" data-end="3550"><strong data-start="3449" data-end="3467">Samson’s Hair:</strong> fine-scale coefficient, visible marker of identity, cut to suppress recognition.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3551" data-end="3713">
<p data-start="3553" data-end="3713"><strong data-start="3553" data-end="3575">Gethsemane Escape:</strong> multiscale diversion — garment (visible), hair (identity), greeting (context) — coefficients peeled away to slip out of representation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3714" data-end="3823">
<p data-start="3716" data-end="3823"><strong data-start="3716" data-end="3730">The Sower:</strong> surplus distributed across scales, yielding abundantly when planted in fertile resolution.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3825" data-end="3828">
<h3 data-start="3830" data-end="3889">Conclusion: Consciousness as Multiresolution Analysis</h3>
<p data-start="3890" data-end="4129">Wavelet theory shows that <em data-start="3916" data-end="3923">iqraʾ</em> is not a single command but a spectrum of operations: read, conceal, collect, broadcast, retain, delay, and warn. Consciousness is multiscale not only in time and frequency but in ethics and concealment.</p>
<p data-start="4131" data-end="4383">In algebra, the balance is at one scale. In harmonics, resonance is across frequencies. In wavelets, consciousness learns to shift scales, pruning or amplifying, concealing or revealing, until the surplus can be faithfully reconstructed in awareness.</p>
<hr data-start="4385" data-end="4388">
