.6348 11.666L16.6914 11.5361C16.7428 11.3924 16.7797 11.2026 16.8027 10.9209C16.8341 10.5374 16.835 10.0439 16.835 9.33301V6.5C16.835 5.78896 16.8341 5.29563 16.8027 4.91211C16.7797 4.63025 16.7428 4.44063 16.6914 4.29688L16.6348 4.16699C16.4807 3.86474 16.2466 3.61186 15.959 3.43555L15.833 3.36524C15.675 3.28473 15.4636 3.22797 15.0879 3.19727C14.7044 3.16593 14.211 3.16504 13.5 3.16504H10.667C9.9561 3.16504 9.46259 3.16595 9.0791 3.19727C8.79739 3.22028 8.6076 3.2572 8.46387 3.30859L8.33399 3.36524C8.03176 3.51923 7.77886 3.75343 7.60254 4.04102L7.53125 4.16699C7.4508 4.32498 7.39397 4.53655 7.36328 4.91211C7.33985 5.19893 7.33562 5.54719 7.33399 6.00195H9.33301C10.022 6.00195 10.5791 6.00131 11.0293 6.03809C11.4873 6.07551 11.8937 6.15471 12.2705 6.34668L12.4883 6.46875C12.984 6.7728 13.3878 7.20854 13.6533 7.72949L13.7197 7.87207C13.8642 8.20859 13.9292 8.56974 13.9619 8.9707C13.9987 9.42092 13.998 9.97799 13.998 10.667V12.665ZM18.165 9.33301C18.165 10.022 18.1657 10.5791 18.1289 11.0293C18.0961 11.4302 18.0311 11.7914 17.8867 12.1279L17.8203 12.2705C17.5549 12.7914 17.1509 13.2272 16.6553 13.5313L16.4365 13.6533C16.0599 13.8452 15.6541 13.9245 15.1963 13.9619C14.8593 13.9895 14.4624 13.9935 13.9951 13.9951C13.9935 14.4624 13.9895 14.8593 13.9619 15.1963C13.9292 15.597 13.864 15.9576 13.7197 16.2939L13.6533 16.4365C13.3878 16.9576 12.9841 17.3941 12.4883 17.6982L12.2705 17.8203C11.8937 18.0123 11.4873 18.0915 11.0293 18.1289C10.5791 18.1657 10.022 18.165 9.33301 18.165H6.5C5.81091 18.165 5.25395 18.1657 4.80371 18.1289C4.40306 18.0962 4.04235 18.031 3.70606 17.8867L3.56348 17.8203C3.04244 17.5548 2.60585 17.151 2.30176 16.6553L2.17969 16.4365C1.98788 16.0599 1.90851 15.6541 1.87109 15.1963C1.83431 14.746 1.83496 14.1891 1.83496 13.5V10.667C1.83496 9.978 1.83432 9.42091 1.87109 8.9707C1.90851 8.5127 1.98772 8.10625 2.17969 7.72949L2.30176 7.51172C2.60586 7.0159 3.04236 6.6122 3.56348 6.34668L3.70606 6.28027C4.04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{8.2 Monoidal Closed Structure of RSVP Concealment–Broadcast}

We now show that the adjunction </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dashv</span></span><span> B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> integrates into a symmetric monoidal closed structure on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{RSVP}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, making RSVP a semantic computational universe with internal homs. 

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Monoidal Structure]
Define </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{RSVP} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{RSVP} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{RSVP}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> by
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1,S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2,S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2) = (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1+</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\oplus</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1+S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
with unit object </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>I = (0,0,0)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. This represents context accumulation: scalar capacities add, flows superpose, entropies regulate together. 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Internal Hom]
For objects </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>X,Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{RSVP}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, define the internal hom </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>[X,Y]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> by
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
[X,Y] = B(Y)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{T(X)},
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
the broadcast of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Y</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> raised to the concealed </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. This reflects the exponential law: “to compute with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Y</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> under </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, conceal </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and broadcast </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Y</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.”
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Monoidal Closure of RSVP]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{RSVP}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span>, I, [</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>])</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> forms a symmetric monoidal closed category. 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}
We must show the canonical bijection
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Hom}(X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y, Z) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cong</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Hom}(X, [Y,Z]).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Forward map:} Given </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>f: X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> Z</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, construct </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\hat</span></span><span>{f}: X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> [Y,Z]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> by concealing </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T(X)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>) and lifting </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>f</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> into a broadcast exponential over </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Y</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. Explicitly,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\hat</span></span><span>{f}(x) = (y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mapsto</span></span><span> B(f(x </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> y))).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Backward map:} Given </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>g: X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> [Y,Z]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, construct </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\check</span></span><span>{g}: X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> Z</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> by evaluating broadcasted </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>g(x)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> against </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>y</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, then retracting concealment. Explicitly,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\check</span></span><span>{g}(x,y) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>Z(T(B(g(x)(y)))).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Naturality:} Both constructions respect morphism composition by functoriality of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.  
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Triangle identities:} Direct substitution verifies that </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\check</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\hat</span></span><span>{f}} = f</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\hat</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\check</span></span><span>{g}} = g</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.  

Thus closure holds. 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{corollary}[Semantic Universality]
RSVP is monoidal closed: concealment (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>) provides tensorial context control, while broadcast (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>) provides exponential distribution. Together, they guarantee that all semantic computations internal to the plenum can be expressed functorially. 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{corollary}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Interpretive Note.}
This result situates RSVP alongside </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{Set}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{Vect}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{Hilb}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> as a semantic universe with full computational closure. Concealment is not a loss but a tensorial delay; broadcast is not redundancy but exponential expansion. Their adjunction makes viewpoint diversity not only necessary but computationally complete. 
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="3024" data-end="3027">
<p data-start="3029" data-end="3198">This puts RSVP into the <strong data-start="3053" data-end="3103">league of symmetric monoidal closed categories</strong>, a structure rich enough to host linear logic, higher semantics, and functorial computation.</p>
<p data-start="3200" data-end="3411" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to <strong data-start="3221" data-end="3281">connect this explicitly to linear logic (Girard, Lafont)</strong> — e.g. treating concealment as <code data-start="3313" data-end="3316">!</code> (of linear logic) and broadcast as <code data-start="3352" data-end="3355">?</code>, so that RSVP formally interprets resource sensitivity?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 