245 15.1963 13.9619C14.8593 13.9895 14.4624 13.9935 13.9951 13.9951C13.9935 14.4624 13.9895 14.8593 13.9619 15.1963C13.9292 15.597 13.864 15.9576 13.7197 16.2939L13.6533 16.4365C13.3878 16.9576 12.9841 17.3941 12.4883 17.6982L12.2705 17.8203C11.8937 18.0123 11.4873 18.0915 11.0293 18.1289C10.5791 18.1657 10.022 18.165 9.33301 18.165H6.5C5.81091 18.165 5.25395 18.1657 4.80371 18.1289C4.40306 18.0962 4.04235 18.031 3.70606 17.8867L3.56348 17.8203C3.04244 17.5548 2.60585 17.151 2.30176 16.6553L2.17969 16.4365C1.98788 16.0599 1.90851 15.6541 1.87109 15.1963C1.83431 14.746 1.83496 14.1891 1.83496 13.5V10.667C1.83496 9.978 1.83432 9.42091 1.87109 8.9707C1.90851 8.5127 1.98772 8.10625 2.17969 7.72949L2.30176 7.51172C2.60586 7.0159 3.04236 6.6122 3.56348 6.34668L3.70606 6.28027C4.04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{8.2 Monoidal Closed Structure, Internal Homs, and Monoidal Adjunction}

We extend the categorical layer by endowing </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{RSVP}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with a symmetric monoidal </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{closed} structure. 
Intuitively, parallel composition </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> models independent subsystems (e.g., panes/sessions), 
while the internal hom </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>[A,B]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> represents </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{controllers} (pipelines) from </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>A</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> to </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> that are themselves objects of the plenum.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Symmetric Monoidal Closed Category]
A category </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span>,I)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{symmetric monoidal closed} if for every </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>A</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Ob}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, 
the functor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>A</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> -</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> has a right adjoint </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>[-,A]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, i.e., there is a natural isomorphism
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Hom}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}}(X</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> A,B)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cong</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Hom}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}}(X,[A,B]),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
natural in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and equipped with symmetry, associativity, and unit constraints.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{construction}[Internal Hom as Bounded Controllers]
Given RSVP objects </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>A=(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>A,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>A,S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>A)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>B=(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>B,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>B,S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>B)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, define </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>[A,B]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> to be the object of </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{admissible pipelines} from </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>A</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> to </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
[A,B] := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> f:A</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> B </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span>|</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> f </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ is RSVP-lawful, } </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>f</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{effort}}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leq</span></span><span> C, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> H(f)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ bounded}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span>,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
with plenum structure inherited pointwise and bounds </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(C,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> H)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> fixed (or drawn from a size index). 
Evaluation is the RSVP morphism
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{ev}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{A,B} : A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> [A,B] </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\longrightarrow</span></span><span> B,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> (a,f) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mapsto</span></span><span> f(a).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Currying </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Lambda</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and uncurrying are defined via the universal property of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>[A,B]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{construction}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Monoidal Closedness of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{RSVP}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>]
With the above construction and standard coherence maps </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, the category </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{RSVP}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is symmetric monoidal closed.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}[Proof Sketch]
(1) </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is given by parallel product of plenum states and morphisms, with RSVP dynamics acting componentwise and no cross-talk by default.  
(2) For each </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>A</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, define </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>[A,-]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> as above; the bijection </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Hom}(X</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> A,B)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cong</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Hom}(X,[A,B])</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is given by currying/uncurrying using </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{ev}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.  
(3) Naturality and coherence follow from functoriality of RSVP morphisms, boundedness closure under composition, and standard monoidal coherence (Mac Lane). 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Monoidal Structure on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>]
A functor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>F:(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span>,I)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span>,I)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{lax monoidal} if it is equipped with structure maps 
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{X,Y}:F(X)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> F(Y)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> F(X</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0:I</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> F(I)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> satisfying coherence; 
it is </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{strong monoidal} if these are isomorphisms. 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[Concealment is Strong Monoidal; Broadcast is Lax Monoidal]
The concealment functor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is strong monoidal, with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T(X</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cong</span></span><span> T(X)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> T(Y)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T(I)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cong</span></span><span> I</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. 
The broadcast functor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is lax monoidal with canonical maps </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>B(X)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> B(Y)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> B(X</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> induced by synchronized downtree overlays.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}[Proof Sketch]
Concealment scales entropy locally and independently, hence distributes strictly over </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. 
Broadcast introduces global overlays that may couple components, hence only yields a canonical comparison map, generally non-invertible.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Monoidal Adjunction]
With the structures above, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dashv</span></span><span> B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> upgrades to a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{monoidal adjunction}; i.e., the unit </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and counit </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> are monoidal natural transformations compatible with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and the monoidal constraints.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}[Proof Sketch]
Check that </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> commute with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> up to the given structure maps, and verify the monoidal triangle identities. 
Naturality is inherited from the base adjunction (Section 8.1) and compatibility with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> from the previous proposition.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\medskip</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{8.3 Strong Monad and Comonad; Eilenberg--Moore Perspectives}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{corollary}[Strong Concealment Monad; Lax Broadcast Comonad]
The adjunction </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dashv</span></span><span> B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> induces a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{strong} monad </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{T},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eta</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mu</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{T}=B</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and strength 
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{X,Y}:X</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{T}Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{T}(X</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>; and a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{lax} comonad </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{B},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{B}=T</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{corollary}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Algebras and Coalgebras]
An Eilenberg--Moore </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-algebra </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(A,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{T}A</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> A)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a state with a specified </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{policy of de-concealment}; 
a </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{B}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-coalgebra </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(C,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>:C</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{B}C)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a state with a specified </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{policy of broadcast persistence}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[CTM as Mixed (Co)algebraic Structure]
CTM stages instantiate </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-algebras (how concealed chunks re-enter STM) and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{B}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-coalgebras (how broadcasts persist across LTM), yielding a bialgebraic view of attention/inspection.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\medskip</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{8.4 Traced/Dagger Structure and Feedback}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Traced Symmetric Monoidal Category]
A symmetric monoidal category </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span>,I)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{traced} if for each triple </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(X,Y,Z)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> there is an operation 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{Z}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{X,Y}:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Hom}(X</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z, Y</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Hom}(X,Y)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
satisfying yanking, vanishing, sliding, and superposing axioms.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[Feedback as Trace]
RSVP feedback loops (e.g., recurrent inspection cycles, closed-loop control) are modeled by </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>; the yanking axiom expresses the </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{no-op} of a concealed identity loop, matching CTM’s unconscious link elision.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Dagger Compact Structure (Optional)]
If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> admits a dagger functor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dagger</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and compact structure (cups/caps), undo/redo and time reversal of pipelines become well-typed morphisms, useful for formalizing reversible edits and inverse broadcasts.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\medskip</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{8.5 Enrichment and Lawvere-Metric Semantics}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Quantitative Enrichment]
Enrich </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> over the Lawvere quantale </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>([0,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>],</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\geq</span></span><span>,+,0)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> by assigning to each hom-set a cost metric 
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>d(f,g)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span>[0,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (e.g., effort or free-energy gap), with composition subadditive and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> bilipschitz.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[Continuity of Concealment and Broadcast]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> are (co)nonexpansive with respect to the enrichment: 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
d(Tf,Tg)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leq</span></span><span> d(f,g),</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> d(Bf,Bg)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leq</span></span><span> L</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> d(f,g) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ for some }L</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ge</span></span><span> 1.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{corollary}[Fixed Points and Stability]
If a pipeline </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>p</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> satisfies </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>d(p,BTp)=0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, then </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>p</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a fixed point of the concealment–broadcast cycle; such points correspond to </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{stable conscious routines} (resonant macros) in CTM/RSVP.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{corollary}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\medskip</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{8.6 Summary of the Categorical Layer}
We have:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> A symmetric monoidal closed </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{RSVP}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with internal hom </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>[A,B]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (controllers as objects).
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> A monoidal adjunction </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dashv</span></span><span> B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, yielding a strong monad </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{T}=BT</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and a lax comonad </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{B}=TB</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Traced structure modeling feedback; optional dagger-compact structure for reversible edits.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Quantitative enrichment (Lawvere metric) connecting costs/entropy/free energy with morphism semantics.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}
This completes the categorical foundation promised by the Theorem of Viewpoint Diversity and integrates seamlessly with the CTM mapping and RSVP PDEs introduced earlier.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.