01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>*{Appendix A: Formal Proof Sketch of the RSVP Crystalline Reset}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.1 Assumptions and Setting}

Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> be a compact smooth </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-manifold without boundary (e.g., the flat torus </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>) endowed with the standard volume form </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>dx</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. 
Consider the RSVP fields </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},S): </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> [0,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>n </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ge</span></span><span> 0}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> satisfying
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{equation}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{eq:rsvp-appendix}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{aligned}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}) </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>= -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span> S, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>&gt;0, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v} + (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>= -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> S, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span>&gt;0, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t S + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>(S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}) </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>= </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span>&gt;0,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{aligned}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{equation}
with smooth initial data </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0,S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and periodic boundary conditions (equivalently, zero-flux for all conserved currents). 
Denote spatial average by </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{f} := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{1}{|</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>|}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} f</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>dx</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

We posit a coercive Lyapunov functional (free-energy-like):
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{equation}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{eq:energy}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{E}(t) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Big</span></span><span>( </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tfrac</span></span><span>{1}{2}|</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}|</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 + U(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>) + V(S) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Big</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> dx,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{equation}
where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>U,V</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> are </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>C</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> convex with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>U''(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>),V''(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ge</span></span><span> c</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0&gt;0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and grow at least quadratically. This enforces a priori bounds on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and (by convexity) in higher </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>p</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> norms when needed.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.2 Entropy Decay}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{lemma}[Global </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-decay of entropy]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{lem:S-L1-decay}
Under </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eqref</span></span><span>{eq:rsvp-appendix} and compactness of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{d}{dt}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> dx = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> dx - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> dx.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Since </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> dx = 0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (periodic boundary), it follows that
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{d}{dt}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1} = - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span>}{|</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>|}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Hence </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>S(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>,t)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> decays to </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with rate </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gtrsim</span></span><span> 1/t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{lemma}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}[Proof sketch]
Integrate the </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-equation over </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and use divergence theorem (flux vanishes). Jensen/Sobolev yield </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ge</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2/|</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>|</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, which gives the differential inequality and decay by standard ODE comparison.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{lemma}[Energy dissipation and boundedness]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{lem:energy}
Assuming the momentum equation admits the standard energy identity,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{d}{dt}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tfrac</span></span><span>{1}{2}|</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}|</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> dx = - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> dx + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> dx,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
