We record a Fourier-mode (torus) analysis that yields </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{exponential} convergence to crystalline states when the entropy dissipation parameter </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> dominates advection/feedback, i.e., a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{spectral gap} exists. We also sketch a stable semi-implicit scheme suitable for numerical illustration.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>*{A.7.1 Linearization about a Crystalline State}

Fix a crystalline base state </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>,S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>)=(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}},0)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>}=0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}}=0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. Let
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span>:=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{u}:=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> s:=S-0=S.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Linearizing </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eqref</span></span><span>{eq:rsvp-appendix} and dropping quadratic terms gives (on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{equation}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{eq:lin}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span> = -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{u}) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\equiv</span></span><span> -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{u},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{u} = -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span> + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> s,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span>
