</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n+1} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>= </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n} - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>h</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n}),</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n+1} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>= </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n} - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>h)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n} - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>h </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n+1} + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>h S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n+1},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n+1} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>= S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n} + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>h </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n+1} - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n+1},
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{align*}
where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>h,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>h</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> are centered differences. The </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-update is implicit in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, giving
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n+1} = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n} + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>h </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n+1}}{1+</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> t}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
A Courant-type condition on the explicit advection terms suffices for stability:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{CFL}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> x}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{CFL}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span>(0,1),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
while the implicit </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> grants unconditional damping of entropy. In the spectral-gap regime (Proposition~</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ref</span></span><span>{prop:gap}), the discrete solution converges exponentially to the discrete crystal at a rate </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\min</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> c</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{-1}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> up to discretization error.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>*{A.7.4 Practical Criterion}

In practice, an effective sufficient condition is
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gtrsim</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> 2</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sqrt</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>}+</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{2</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>}{L},
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
on an </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-torus of side length </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, ensuring that the first nonzero Fourier shell is strictly damped with margin. Tuning </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> modifies only the threshold; once satisfied, the crystalline reset proceeds at an exponential rate governed by </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\medskip</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\noindent</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Summary.} A simple Fourier analysis furnishes a clean spectral-gap condition guaranteeing exponential decay of all nonzero modes, thereby sharpening Appendix~A’s asymptotic smoothing to </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{exponential} crystalline convergence in a physically transparent parameter regime (large </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> relative to feedback and advection).
