</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Evolutionary Hypotheses of the Universe}

The idea that universes may undergo a process of reproduction, inheritance, and selection
was first framed in physics by Wheeler’s notion of ``law without law'' and his concept
of universes budding from black holes </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\citep</span></span><span>{wheeler1977observer}. 
Smolin formalized this as the theory of Cosmological Natural Selection, where black holes
serve as reproductive sites transmitting slightly varied fundamental constants
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\citep</span></span><span>{smolin1997cosmosLife}. Carr later collected a range of fine-tuning perspectives
in his edited volume </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\citep</span></span><span>{carr2009multiverse}.

Recent work has revisited these themes from biological and informational standpoints.
Julian Gough’s *Egg and the Rock Project* casts universes as organisms evolving in complexity,
where fine-tuned constants act as adaptive traits </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\citep</span></span><span>{gough2024egg,gough2025podcast}. 
Chris Fields has proposed that such cosmological processes are best modeled as
scale-free informational systems, with parallels to individuation in physics and biology
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\citep</span></span><span>{fields2021info,fields2023chapter13}. Michael Levin has argued that cognition and
goal-directedness are not emergent late features of biology but extend downward to
all self-organizing matter, offering a bridge between cosmological selection and embodied agency
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\citep</span></span><span>{levin2022cognition}.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{RSVP Formalism and the Reset Hypothesis}

Within RSVP, the governing PDEs
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> = -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}) - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span> S,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v} = -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> S,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t S = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
predict that entropy drives the plenum toward uniform crystalline states, 
not bounces. Thus, RSVP differs from cosmological natural selection by 
proposing that the universe does not proliferate via black hole “offspring” but instead 
resets after a Poincaré recurrence time into a highly ordered low-entropy state.  
This crystalline reset is an attractor of the dynamics and rules out oscillatory 
universes, which are exponentially unstable under entropy flow.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Empirical Hints and Analogies}

JWST observations of early galaxy and black hole formation already suggest rapid
self-organization of structure, consistent with evolutionary and RSVP interpretations
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\citep</span></span><span>{jwst2023early}. NASA’s cultural and scientific reflections on cosmic context
underscore how these ideas connect to broader frameworks of meaning
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\citep</span></span><span>{nasa2015cosmosculture}. From an epistemological angle, Roderick’s analysis of analogy
frames such cross-domain mappings as fundamental to knowledge itself
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\citep</span></span><span>{roderick2016analogy}.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Synthesis}

RSVP agrees with the cosmological natural selection literature that 
fine-tuned constants and ``quirks'' of physics should not be seen as coincidences.
Where it diverges is in rejecting the reproductive-Darwinian metaphor 
in favor of entropic smoothing and crystalline reset. 
Universes do not breed; they dissolve, smooth, and reset.  
The recurrence-based reset mechanism preserves lawlike structure without invoking 
a proliferating multiverse.

In this way, RSVP offers a parsimonious alternative:
cosmological fine-tuning arises from long-timescale entropic smoothing 
rather than inter-universal competition.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
