ext-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="249">Got it. Based on the structure of your monograph and the depth of topics, here’s a <strong data-start="83" data-end="127">new, expanded outline for the appendices</strong> that integrates your earlier draft but broadens scope and coherence across philology, math, computation, and artifacts:</p>
<hr data-start="251" data-end="254">
<h1 data-start="256" data-end="302">Appendices Outline for <em data-start="281" data-end="302">Viewpoint Diversity</em></h1>
<h3 data-start="304" data-end="381">Appendix A: Philological Notes (Hebrew, Greek, Arabic, Cross-Tradition)</h3>
<ul data-start="382" data-end="923">
<li data-start="382" data-end="518">
<p data-start="384" data-end="518"><strong data-start="384" data-end="395">Hebrew:</strong> Job 31:33 and concealment; semantic range of <em data-start="441" data-end="448">kasah</em> (to cover), comparison with ritual hygiene and scribal concealment.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="519" data-end="639">
<p data-start="521" data-end="639"><strong data-start="521" data-end="531">Greek:</strong> The <em data-start="536" data-end="558">Parable of the Sower</em>; semantic depth of <em data-start="578" data-end="597">logos spermatikos</em> and seed metaphors in early philosophy.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="640" data-end="753">
<p data-start="642" data-end="753"><strong data-start="642" data-end="653">Arabic:</strong> <em data-start="654" data-end="661">Iqraʾ</em> and its seven meanings; connection to <em data-start="700" data-end="709">al-jabr</em> (restoration) and <em data-start="728" data-end="738">muqābala</em> (balancing).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="754" data-end="923">
<p data-start="756" data-end="923"><strong data-start="756" data-end="776">Cross-tradition:</strong> Parallels in Buddhist <em data-start="799" data-end="818">pratītyasamutpāda</em>, Hindu <em data-start="826" data-end="831">ṛta</em>, and Indigenous narrative structures.<br data-start="869" data-end="872">
<em data-start="872" data-end="923">(6–8 pages, with tables of cognates and glosses.)</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="925" data-end="928">
<h3 data-start="930" data-end="1008">Appendix B: Full Equations and Proofs (PCT, Active Inference, CTM, RSVP)</h3>
<ul data-start="1009" data-end="1446">
<li data-start="1009" data-end="1083">
<p data-start="1011" data-end="1083"><strong data-start="1011" data-end="1031">PCT derivations:</strong> feedback control equations, stability conditions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1084" data-end="1162">
<p data-start="1086" data-end="1162"><strong data-start="1086" data-end="1107">Active Inference:</strong> free-energy minimization proofs, variational bounds.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1163" data-end="1248">
<p data-start="1165" data-end="1248"><strong data-start="1165" data-end="1183">CTM formalism:</strong> uptree competition theorem, broadcast axiom, inspection axiom.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1249" data-end="1446">
<p data-start="1251" data-end="1446"><strong data-start="1251" data-end="1265">RSVP PDEs:</strong> full derivations, Fourier analysis of entropy smoothing, torsion suppression, and proof of the RSVP Theorem of Viewpoint Diversity.<br data-start="1397" data-end="1400">
<em data-start="1400" data-end="1446">(8–12 pages, heavy in equations and proofs.)</em></p>
</li>
