ng> without altering your voice. Here are improvements section by section:</p>
<hr data-start="316" data-end="319">
<h3 data-start="321" data-end="349"><strong data-start="325" data-end="349">General improvements</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="350" data-end="763">
<li data-start="350" data-end="480">
<p data-start="352" data-end="480">Add <strong data-start="356" data-end="379">short introductions</strong> at the start of each appendix, so they read like self-contained mini-essays rather than raw notes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="481" data-end="649">
<p data-start="483" data-end="649">Where possible, include <strong data-start="507" data-end="538">forward/backward references</strong> (e.g., “as discussed in Chapter 4” or “see also Appendix F”), so appendices remain woven into the monograph.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="650" data-end="763">
<p data-start="652" data-end="763">In proofs/equations, include <strong data-start="681" data-end="705">interpretive remarks</strong> to bridge formal math with your conceptual scaffolding.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="765" data-end="768">
<h3 data-start="770" data-end="808"><strong data-start="774" data-end="808">Appendix A: Philological Notes</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="809" data-end="1422">
<li data-start="809" data-end="1036">
<p data-start="811" data-end="847">Add a <strong data-start="817" data-end="833">framing note</strong> at the top:</p>
<blockquote data-start="850" data-end="1036">
<p data-start="852" data-end="1036">“This appendix demonstrates how ancient terms encode multi-layered meanings, serving as proto-algorithms of concealment, revelation, and balance, which are later formalized in RSVP.”</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
<li data-start="1037" data-end="1153">
<p data-start="1039" data-end="1153">In <em data-start="1042" data-end="1050">Hebrew</em> section: emphasize <strong data-start="1070" data-end="1106">parallel with entropy thresholds</strong> — concealment as structural, not just moral.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1154" data-end="1277">
<p data-start="1156" data-end="1277">In <em data-start="1159" data-end="1166">Greek</em> section: note how <em data-start="1185" data-end="1204">logos spermatikos</em> anticipates information-theoretic notions of seed as minimal encoding.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1278" data-end="1422">
<p data-start="1280" data-end="1422">In <em data-start="1283" data-end="1291">Arabic</em> section: after the list, explicitly tie to <strong data-start="1335" data-end="1353">control theory</strong>: “delay” = buffer, “retain” = memory, “warn” = actuator broadcast.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1424" data-end="1427">
<h3 data-start="1429" data-end="1474"><strong data-start="1433" data-end="1474">Appendix B: Full Equations and Proofs</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1475" data-end="1873">
<li data-start="1475" data-end="1553">
<p data-start="1477" data-end="1553">Add explicit <strong data-start="1490" data-end="1516">numbering of equations</strong> so later references can cite them.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1554" data-end="1742">
<p data-start="1556" data-end="1618">After each derivation, add <strong data-start="1583" data-end="1610">interpretive paragraphs</strong>: e.g.</p>
<blockquote data-start="1621" data-end="1742">
<p data-start="1623" data-end="1742">“Equation (B.3) shows the RSVP PDE’s entropy term acting as a regulator, analogous to PCT’s error minimization loop.”</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
<li data-start="1743" data-end="1873">
<p data-start="1745" data-end="1873">Consider a <strong data-start="1756" data-end="1771">short table</strong> comparing “Control Theory vs. Active Inference vs. CTM vs. RSVP” to highlight structural analogies.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1875" data-end="1878">
<h3 data-start="1880" data-end="1924"><strong data-start="1884" data-end="1924">Appendix C: Computational Complexity</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1925" data-end="2316">
<li data-start="1925" data-end="2150">
<p data-start="1927" data-end="1969">Add one or two <strong data-start="1942" data-end="1966">examples of problems</strong>:</p>
<blockquote data-start="1972" data-end="2150">
<p data-start="1974" data-end="2150">“Reconstructing a global RSVP state from partial observations is analogous to graph coloring or satisfiability: computationally feasible only if entropy constraints are low.”</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
<li data-start="2151" data-end="2316">
<p data-start="2153" data-end="2193">Expand the information-theory section:</p>
<ul data-start="2196" data-end="2316">
<li data-start="2196" data-end="2243">
<p data-start="2198" data-end="2243">Relate $\theta(S)$ to <strong data-start="2220" data-end="2240">channel capacity</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2246" data-end="2316">
<p data-start="2248" data-end="2316">Note that concealment = lossy coding → scarcity of interpretation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2318" data-end="2321">
<h3 data-start="2323" data-end="2366"><strong data-start="2327" data-end="2366">Appendix D: Catalogue Entry — CORAN</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2367" data-end="2618">
<li data-start="2367" data-end="2502">
<p data-start="2369" data-end="2502">Add <strong data-start="2373" data-end="2399">figural interpretation</strong>: the 3×2×19 proportions could be linked to <strong data-start="2443" data-end="2471">Metonic cycle ≈ 19 years</strong> and calendrical mathematics.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2503" data-end="2618">
<p data-start="2505" data-end="2618">Note the <strong data-start="2514" data-end="2530">mnemonic pun</strong>: “CORAN” (as acronym) vs. “Qurʾān” (recitation), playing with concealment/disclosure.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2620" data-end="2623">
<h3 data-start="2625" data-end="2649"><strong data-start="2629" data-end="2649">Appendix E: Poem</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2650" data-end="2947">
<li data-start="2650" data-end="2837">
<p data-start="2652" data-end="2687">Add an <strong data-start="2659" data-end="2684">introductory sentence</strong>:</p>
<blockquote data-start="2690" data-end="2837">
<p data-start="2692" data-end="2837">“This poem was first drafted as an interpretive gloss on the seven meanings of <em data-start="2771" data-end="2778">iqraʾ</em>, structuring philology into verse as mnemonic encoding.”</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
<li data-start="2838" data-end="2947">
<p data-start="2840" data-end="2947">Include a <strong data-start="2850" data-end="2885">short commentary for each verse</strong> (even one sentence each) rather than one general paragraph.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2949" data-end="2952">
<h3 data-start="2954" data-end="2989"><strong data-start="2958" data-end="2989">Appendix F: Macros and Code</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2990" data-end="3252">
<li data-start="2990" data-end="3154">
<p data-start="2992" data-end="3006">Add context:</p>
<blockquote data-start="3009" data-end="3154">
<p data-start="3011" data-end="3154">“These macros and snippets are designed to ensure reproducibility of RSVP simulations across LaTeX manuscripts and toy computational models.”</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
<li data-start="3155" data-end="3252">
<p data-start="3157" data-end="3252">Expand the code: show <strong data-start="3179" data-end="3201">visualization step</strong> (e.g., mapping $\Phi, \mathbf{v}, S$ to colors).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3254" data-end="3257">
<h3 data-start="3259" data-end="3306"><strong data-start="3263" data-end="3306">Appendix G: Mathematical Infrastructure</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="3307" data-end="3547">
<li data-start="3307" data-end="3456">
<p data-start="3309" data-end="3333">Strengthen connection:</p>
<ul data-start="3336" data-end="3456">
<li data-start="3336" data-end="3374">
<p data-start="3338" data-end="3374">Category → constraint composition.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3377" data-end="3408">
<p data-start="3379" data-end="3408">Sheaf → concealment/gluing.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3411" data-end="3456">
<p data-start="3413" data-end="3456">Topology → recurrence and spectral reset.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="3457" data-end="3547">
<p data-start="3459" data-end="3547">Add <strong data-start="3463" data-end="3488">one worked mini-proof</strong> of sheaf gluing lemma (tying back to main RSVP Theorem).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3549" data-end="3552">
<h3 data-start="3554" data-end="3599"><strong data-start="3558" data-end="3599">Appendix H: Bibliographic Annotations</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="3600" data-end="3944">
<li data-start="3600" data-end="3801">
<p data-start="3602" data-end="3678">Expand to include <strong data-start="3620" data-end="3641">publication years</strong> and a sentence per entry. Example:</p>
<blockquote data-start="3681" data-end="3801">
<p data-start="3683" data-end="3801">“Alter (2010): his translation of Job highlights concealment as thematic; indispensable for philological grounding.”</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
<li data-start="3802" data-end="3944">
<p data-start="3804" data-end="3944">Add a few <strong data-start="3814" data-end="3840">non-Western references</strong> (e.g., Buddhist sutras, Vedic texts, Indigenous cosmologies), since you reference them in Appendix A.</p>
</li>
</ul>
