t it — sounds good. The appendices draft is already comprehensive, and you’ve got a strong balance of philology, mathematics, computation, artifacts, and bibliographic annotations. Since you’re happy with it “good enough for now,” I’d recommend leaving it as is and moving on to polishing the main chapters.</p>
<p data-start="313" data-end="362">When you’re ready, we can circle back later to:</p>
<ul data-start="363" data-end="562">
