normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="188">If you want something in the vein of <strong data-start="37" data-end="57">“syncretization”</strong> but also signalling that the work is <em data-start="95" data-end="114">still in progress</em>, here are some two-word commit message options that might capture both:</p>
<ul data-start="190" data-end="625">
<li data-start="190" data-end="248">
<p data-start="192" data-end="248"><strong data-start="192" data-end="213">“Syncretic Draft”</strong> – signals fusion + incompletion.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="249" data-end="319">
<p data-start="251" data-end="319"><strong data-start="251" data-end="279">“Partial Syncretization”</strong> – technical tone, clearly unfinished.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="320" data-end="383">
<p data-start="322" data-end="383"><strong data-start="322" data-end="350">“Syncretization Pending”</strong> – work is underway, not final.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="384" data-end="446">
<p data-start="386" data-end="446"><strong data-start="386" data-end="418">“Provisional Syncretization”</strong> – careful, academic feel.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="447" data-end="507">
<p data-start="449" data-end="507"><strong data-start="449" data-end="473">“Fragmentary Fusion”</strong> – more poetic, but still clear.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="508" data-end="557">
<p data-start="510" data-end="557"><strong data-start="510" data-end="536">“Incomplete Synthesis”</strong> – plain, accurate.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="558" data-end="625">
<p data-start="560" data-end="625"><strong data-start="560" data-end="586">“Rough Syncretization”</strong> – signals active merging, but rough.</p>
</li>
